</div><div class="html-p">It is concluded that <span class="html-italic">V<sub>cm</sub></span> is equal to <span class="html-italic">V<sub>pv</sub></span>/2 in all four modes. Hence, this constant <span class="html-italic">V<sub>cm</sub></span> results in nullifying the leakage current in this proposed H6 inverter. Secondly, conduction loss is reduced since only two switches conduct during the active mode of the negative half cycle of the grid voltage. This enhances the efficiency of inverter circuit.</div><section id="ControlStrategy" type=""><h4 class="html-italic" data-nested="2" style="font-family: Arial, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">  Control Strategy</h4><div class="html-p">The control strategy employed to generate SPWM pulses is shown in <a href="https://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/15/10/3789#fig_body_display_energies-15-03789-f011" class="html-fig html-figpopup">Figure 11</a>.</div><div class="html-fig-wrap" id="energies-15-03789-f011">
