                    <a href="mailto:?&amp;subject=From%20MDPI%3A%20%22Novel%20H6%20Transformerless%20Inverter%20for%20Grid%20Connected%20Photovoltaic%20System%20to%20Reduce%20the%20Conduction%20Loss%20and%20Enhance%20Efficiency%22&amp;body=https://www.mdpi.com/1641342%3A%0A%0ANovel%20H6%20Transformerless%20Inverter%20for%20Grid%20Connected%20Photovoltaic%20System%20to%20Reduce%20the%20Conduction%20Loss%20and%20Enhance%20EfficiencyPresence%20of%20a%20transformer%20in%20a%20grid%20connected%20photovoltaic%20system%20provides%20galvanic%20isolation%20between%20the%20photovoltaic%20panels%20and%20the%20grid.%20However%2C%20it%20increases%20the%20overall%20cost%2C%20makes%20the%20circuit%20bulky%20and%20reduces%20the%20efficiency%20of%20the%20system.%20Hence%2C%20transformerless%20inverters%20have%20gained%20significant%20importance%20owing%20to%20its%20low%20cost%2C%20light%20weight%20and%20increased%20efficiency.%20However%2C%20due%20to%20the%20absence%20of%20the%20transformer%2C%20there%20is%20no%20galvanic%20isolation%20between%20photovoltaic%20panels%20and%20the%20grid%20and%20there%20is%20always%20a%20threat%20of%20flow%20of%20leakage%20current.%20In%20this%20research%20paper%2C%20an%20elaborate%20analysis%20of%20H4%2C%20H5%20and%20H6%20transformerless%20inverter%20is%20carried%20out.%20DC%20side%20decoupled%20circuits%20are%20studied%20to%20eliminate%20the%20leakage%20current.%20Their%20performances%20are%20compared%20based%20on%20the%20simulations%20carried%20out%20in%20MATLAB%2FSIMULINK%20software.%20A%20novel%20H6%20inverter%20is%20proposed%20by%20introducing%20an%20additional%20switch%20in%20H5%20topology.%20A%20direct%20current%20path%20is%20provided%20in%20H5%20topology%20during%20one%20of%20the%20active%20modes%2C%20so%20that%20current%20flows%20through%20few%20switches%20thereby%20reducing%20the%20conduction%20losses.%20Common%20mode%20voltage%20remains%20constant%20in%20the%20proposed%20H6%20inverter%20and%20hence%20the%20leakage[...]" title="Email">
